    description "Does the science support vaccine mandates for people already naturally infected?&#10;&#10;Short answer, I don't think so&#10;&#10;Today&#10;&#10;Reinfections added to running total of cases, + 800,000&#10;&#10;Therefore, cases higher than previously documented&#10;&#10;Vaccine mandates&#10;&#10;NHS, mandates be scrapped Monday by Sajid Javid&#10;&#10;Omicron Covid variant, now dominant and milder&#10;&#10;Thursday, Feb 3, last day to get first jab for April&#10;&#10;Care home staff have been mandated since November&#10;&#10;40,000 people can now go back to work&#10;&#10;UK must learn to live with Covid&#10;&#10;https://www.nytimes.com/live/2022/01/19/world/omicron-covid-vaccine-tests&#10;&#10;https://www.cms.gov/files/document/qso-22-09-all-injunction-lifted.pdf&#10; &#10;&#10;Health care workers in 24&#10;&#10;10 million workers&#10;&#10;76,000 health care facilities, Medicaid and Medicare program&#10;&#10;Must receive at least one shot within 30 days&#10;&#10;Must be fully vaccinated by March 15&#10;Alabama, Alaska, Arizona, Arkansas, Georgia, Idaho, Indiana, Iowa, Kansas, Kentucky, Louisiana, Mississippi, Missouri, Montana, Nebraska, New Hampshire, North Dakota, Ohio, Oklahoma, South Carolina, South Dakota, Utah, West Virginia, Wyoming&#10;&#10;Timelines already in place for other 25 states, health care workers must by fully vaccinated by Feb. 28&#10;&#10;COVID-19 Cases and Hospitalizations by COVID-19 Vaccination Status and Previous COVID-19 Diagnosis &#8212; California and New York, May&#8211;November 2021&#10;&#10;https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/volumes/71/wr/mm7104e1.htm#contribAff"
