  node [
    id 366
    label "O9yYXXxemPk"
    step 0
    date "2022-07-12T09:54:38Z"
    title "Beijing mandates COVID vaccines in some spaces"
    description "(7 Jul 2022) &#13;&#10;RESTRICTION SUMMARY:&#13;&#10;ASSOCIATED PRESS&#13;&#10;Beijing &#8211; 7 July 2022&#13;&#10;1. Wide of Beijing street &#13;&#10;2. Various of pedestrians &#13;&#10;3. SOUNDBITE (Mandarin) Chen Yumei, Beijing resident: &#13;&#10;&#34;It (the mandate) says people who are not suitable to get vaccinated can be exempt from vaccination. But how do we prove that we are not suitable for this? Who's going to issue a certification for us? You have asked a lot of doctors and they all said you couldn't &#8211; that means you are indeed not suitable for health reasons. But no one dares to give you this certification. I can't force myself to get vaccinated. I'm not going to risk my life.&#34;&#13;&#10;4. SOUNDBITE (Mandarin) Leo Zhang, Beijing resident: &#13;&#10;&#34;If in the future we only have to show proof of vaccination and requirements for COVID tests to be relaxed, it actually will have a smaller impact on everyone. At least for me, it doesn't have a big impact, it's just getting a booster.&#34;&#13;&#10;5. SOUNDBITE (Mandarin) Muzi (Only name given), Beijing resident: &#13;&#10;&#34;If you want to go to these places, you will have to accept this, right? What is the priority? Your health and your life are what come first, right? And for the sake of your life, you should give up things like enjoyment and entertainment. This is a special situation and there's nothing else you can do. We have to cooperate. You can't be having fun while not supporting the policy. That won't work.&#34;&#13;&#10;6. Wide of scooters in the street&#13;&#10;7. SOUNDBITE (Mandarin) Chen Yumei, Beijing resident:&#13;&#10;&#34;For example, the nucleic acid test. If you want to have daily test, we all do it. All of us cooperate. But something like this is too unreasonable.&#34;&#13;&#10;8. Wide of pedestrians &#13;&#10;9. Wide of scooters in the street&#13;&#10;10. SOUNDBITE (Mandarin) Leo Zhang, Beijing resident:&#13;&#10;&#34;I think the main question is not whether people should be vaccinated. What people are questioning is the epidemic prevention policy. It has been three years and people's mindset has changed. Especially as there have been quite a lot of changes recently, making people more anxious. So there are different voices.&#34;&#13;&#10;11. Various of Zhang leaving on his scooter &#13;&#10;STORYLINE: &#13;&#10;The Chinese capital has issued a mandate requiring people to show proof of COVID-19 vaccination before they can enter some public spaces including gyms, museums and libraries, drawing concern from city residents over the sudden policy announcement and its impact on their daily lives.&#13;&#10;The list of public places requiring vaccination does not include restaurants and offices. The mandate will go into effect on Monday, with exceptions available only to those who cannot be vaccinated for health reasons.&#13;&#10;A vaccine mandate is not unusual and some major cities in the U.S. required proof of vaccination for entry into restaurants and bars at some point during the pandemic.&#13;&#10;However, those mandates did not include spaces like libraries. &#13;&#10;In Beijing and other cities across China, many government facilities already required people to show proof of vaccination before entry.&#13;&#10;Chen Yumei, a 48-year-old Beijing resident, said she hasn't been vaccinated yet because she suffered from hives that doctors had said made her unsuitable.&#13;&#10;&#8220;A lot of doctors told me I couldn't, but who's going to give me the certification for an exception? No one dares to give you this certification,&#34; she said.&#13;&#10;&#8220;Something like this is too unreasonable,&#8221; Chen said. &#13;&#10;Another Beijing resident, Leo Zhang, said he was confused whether the new policy meant he needed to get a booster or if two doses were enough. He is planning to get a booster shot as a result.&#13;&#10;It is unclear how Beijing&#8217;s new directive will be implemented given the national policy. &#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Find out more about AP Archive: http://www.aparchive.com/HowWeWork &#13;&#10;Twitter: https://twitter.com/AP_Archive &#13;&#10;Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/APArchives &#8203;&#8203;&#13;&#10;Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/APNews/&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;#covid19 #vaccines #pandemic #vaccination &#10;You can license this story through AP Archive: http://www.aparchive.com/metadata/youtube/a543881872924056a1f944dc419aaf1d"
    channeltitle "AP Archive"
    channelid "UCHTK-2W11Vh1V4uwofOfR4w"
    favcount 0
    viewcount 255
    likecount 5
    commentcount 0
    duration "PT2M24S"
    indegree 0
    cluster 3
    sentiment 0.0
    leftright "C"
    channeltags "Mainstream News"
  ]
